<title>USA: Magnequench Int'l accuses YBM of infringement.</title>
<headline>Magnequench Int'l accuses YBM of infringement.</headline>
<dateline>ANDERSON, Ind. 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Magnequench International Inc said Monday if filed a lawsuit alleging YBM Magnex International Inc and one of its subsidiaries of patent infringement.</p>
<p>In a prepared statement, Magnequench said the lawsuit follows reports of the sale of an unlicensed form of its Neodymium-Iron-Boron magnetic material in the United States. A Magnequench spokesman declined to elaborate, although he said the lawsuit was not &quot;frivolous.&quot;</p>
<p>Magnequench said it holds several patents of such &quot;rare earth&quot; magnetic materials.</p>
<p>YBM Magnex officials were unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
